{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014vWXMgccqpMn4b4274u4Ep","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (30KB). Full output saved to: /Users/brenn/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-6v-yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn-T-brace-batch-wi2srreh/4172dc03-dd8f-4eaf-8eb3-7cefb8efb090/tool-results/b8bzd4b11.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n{\n  \"B01\": {\n    \"gate\": \"G1\",\n    \"title\": \"Minimal tool surface\",\n    \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\",\n    \"requirement\": \"List every built-in tool, MCP server, API, program, and file permission this agent type can use. Give a task-based reason for each. Enforce a role-based allowlist, and check that an unlisted tool can't be called. Don't base allow or approval decisions on hints a server gives about its own tools, such as \\\"read-only.\\\" MCP treats those hints as untrusted unless you trust the server.\",\n    \"not_covered\": [\n      {\n        \"problem\": \"A tool call that skips the MCP gateway or reaches a tool server directly\",\n        \"owner\": \"E06\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"problem\": \"A token or credential with too much access\",\n        \"owner\": \"B02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"problem\": \"Hidden instructions inside a tool's description or schema\",\n        \"owner\": \"E04\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"problem\": \"A tool's description or schema changing after it was approved\",\n        \"owner\": \"E03\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"problem\": \"Lookalike or duplicate tool names across servers\",\n        \"owner\": \"E05\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"na_when\": \"never\",\n    \"checks\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"B01.1\",\n        \"check\": \"Each agent role has one explicit allowlist of tool names, with no wildcard grants such as `*`, `mcp__*`, `Bash(*)`, or `bypassPermissions`.\",\n        \"coverage_required\": true,\n        \"verify\": \"1) Find where each agent is built and tools are passed (`allowed_tools`, `t