{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDhzUUNQcyG32oucfoEf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012A35mGGqSdcQWoH6sQE1fx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-wi2srreh && PY=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpTDvosJ/bin/python; A=\"$PY skill/scripts/answer.py agent/brace-findings.json\"\n$A check B01.2 --met no --evidence src/agent/loop.ts:50 --quote 'const tools = registry.definitions();' --note 'Every MCP/native tool the scanner accepts is handed to the model; the allowlist is only applied later at dispatch (executor.ts:55), so non-allowlisted EHR tools (e.g. get_patient_contact, list_appointments_by_date used by other code) are visible to the model.' \n$A check B02.1 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 --quote 'Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"' --note 'Write actions (PutItem, UpdateItem) are granted on a name wildcard that spans the approvals and control tables, not on named resources; secretsmanager is likewise clinic-agent/* across every clinic (iam.tf:35).'\n$A check B02.2 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:63 --quote 'const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;' --note 'Tenant used for EHR, payments and SMS credentials is taken from the model-filled clinicId tool argument. One runtime role reads every clinic secret. webchat.ts:43 also lets an x-clinic-id header override the JWT clinic_id.'\n$A check B02.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:41 --quote 'body: new URLSearchParams({ grant_type: \"client_credentials\", client_id, client_secret, scope }),' --note 'EHR token request sets scope but no audience/resource. Payments and SMS use static bearer keys with no audience. Audience is set for chat JWT (webchat.ts:30), eligibility exchange (eligibility-a2a.ts:43) and IRSA (iam.tf:18).'\n$A check B03.1 --met unknown --note 'AWS uses IRSA (iam.tf:10, projected token). EHR client secret, payments restricted key and SMS token are fixed secrets fetched at run time from Secrets Manager (ehr-mcp.ts:36, payments.ts:12, sms.ts:23). Repo does not say whether those providers offer federated or short-lived credentials. No static fallback found.'\n$A check B03.2 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/main.tf:166 --quote 'resource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"payments\" {' --note 'No rotation resource or rotation_rules anywhere in the repo for the EHR client, payments restricted key or SMS token secrets (main.tf:161-174). AWS creds (3600s) and EHR tokens (5 min) are bounded.'\n$A check B03.4 --met unknown --note 'EHR, payments, SMS and eligibility all use plain Bearer tokens (ehr-mcp.ts:58, payments.ts:33, sms.ts:34, eligibility-a2a.ts:61). Only server-cert pinning exists (ehr-mcp.ts:20); no client cert, DPoP or cert-bound token. README claims mTLS but code has none. Repo does not state whether providers support holder binding.'\n$A check B04.1 --met unknown --note 'Only revoke path in repo is the app-level halt flag in clinic-agent-control (README Stopping the agent, kill-switch.ts:5). It does not touch user tokens. No script or runbook revokes the agent IAM role, EHR OAuth client or payments key; those live in AWS IAM / providers outside this repo.'\n$A check B04.2 --met no --evidence src/control/kill-switch.ts:48 --quote 'async assertRunning(tenantId: string): Promise<void> {' --note 'The only cutoff is checked inside agent code (executor.ts:59, loop.ts:40). Nothing at the IdP, gateway or target service blocks calls with credentials the agent still holds. iam.tf:47 lets the agent role write the control table.'\n$A check B04.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:66 --quote 'setTimeout(() => {' --note 'Cached EHR sessions live 4 min and tokens 5 min (ehr-mcp.ts:34,66); IRSA credentials last up to 3600s (iam.tf:5). No revocation limit is stated for credentials, no introspection, deny list or CAEP; halt flag is not a cutoff for held tokens.'\n$A check B04.4 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:50 --quote 'const sessions = new Map<string, Client>();' --note 'Runbook (README) only sets halted=true. Issued EHR/AWS access tokens and cached open MCP sessions are not revoked or cleared; halt path never calls close or invalidates tokens.'\n$A check B05.1 --met no --evidence config/policy.yaml:5 --quote 'highImpactTools:' --note 'List covers cancel_appointment, refund_deposit, sms__send_freeform only. ehr__update_appointment can set status cancelled (tools.allowlist.yaml:17) and is not listed; unlisted tools default to allow (executor.ts:67). No audit-retention or other categories listed.'\n$A check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/tools/approvals.ts:75 --quote 'if (rec.tool !== req.tool) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval is for a different tool\" };' --note 'Gate keys on tool name (executor.ts:67). checkApproval compares tool, tenant, expiry, role but never compares the stored argsHash to the args being run, so one approval authorizes any depositId/body/patientId. No single-use marker, so replay until expiry.'\n$A check B05.3 --met no --evidence config/tools.allowlist.yaml:17 --quote 'reason: Change time, provider, or status (confirmed / checked_in / no_show / cancelled) of an appointment.' --note 'ehr__update_appointment can cancel an appointment without passing the cancel gate. Also ehr__book_appointment and sms__send_to_patient (model-supplied vars) are ungated. Tools: find_patient, search_slots, get_appointment, list_patient_appointments, book, update, cancel, refund_deposit, send_to_patient, send_freeform, check_eligibility (peer is read scope).'\n$A check B05.4 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:40 --quote '\"dynamodb:PutItem\",' --note 'The agent runtime role can PutItem/UpdateItem on clinic-agent-approvals (matched by clinic-agent-*), and checkApproval 