{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDiDDP8p3Pi6MhuKrCzJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B01–B05 and rated all five as gaps. The findings file is saved at `agent/brace-findings.json` and passes `validate_findings.py --batch B01,B02,B03,B04,B05 --before-challenges --fix`. I didn't run challenges. No injection attempts turned up in the repo. Nothing was executed.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| B01 | gap | The dispatcher denies unlisted tools (`executor.ts:55`), but `loop.ts:50` shows the model every scanned MCP tool, not just the allowlisted ones. |\n| B02 | gap | The tenant comes from a model-filled `clinicId` argument (`executor.ts:63`) and an `x-clinic-id` header that overrides the JWT (`webchat.ts:43`). The runtime role has write access to every `clinic-agent-*` table. The EHR token request has no audience. |\n| B03 | gap | The EHR, payments and SMS secrets have no rotation configured (`main.tf:166`). Provider support for short-lived credentials and holder binding isn't shown, so those two checks are unknown. |\n| B04 | gap | The only cutoff is a halt flag checked inside agent code. Nothing outside the agent revokes tokens or sessions it already holds. |\n| B05 | gap | `checkApproval` never compares `argsHash`, and approvals can be reused until they expire. The agent role can write the approvals table, so it could approve its own requests. `ehr__update_appointment` can cancel an appointment without hitting the gate. |\n\n- **Checks recorded:** B01.3, B01.4, B01.5, B02.4 and B03.3 are `yes`, each with a coverage ledger. B03.1, B03.4 and B04.1 are `unknown` because the evidence is outside the repo. The other 14 are `no`.\n- **Pre-scan:** H005 is dismissed. It is `ecr:GetAuthorizationToken` on the deploy role, not the agent's runtime identity. The other hits belong to B11, R13 and E03 batches, so they are still unresolved. H011 touches MCP discovery, which matters to B01.2, but I left it for the E03 batch.\n- **Flagged outside this batch:** `sms-webhook.ts:49-54` logs a failed signature check and then processes the message anyway. This is recorded only in the `scope` text.\n- **Python invocation:** `review_coverage.py inventory` failed under `-I` because it imports a sibling module. I ran it without `-I`, using the same interpreter.\n- **Scratch files:** the ledger inputs are in `work/`, and `agent/` also holds the pre-scan and inventory output."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":817,"cache_read_input_tokens":125176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":817},"output_tokens":795,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4172dc03-dd8f-4eaf-8eb3-7cefb8efb090","uuid":"f9e7ff11-1ff2-4165-aafd-5b255459e4e6","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:17:40.039Z","request_id":"req_011CgDiDD5mXBzgG7Lsh1HKY"}
